Sunday afternoon is quiet and relaxed.
I sit on the sofa and open my laptop.
In Mexico it is only eight o'clock in the morning right now.
My family is sitting at the breakfast table right now.
Diego and Sofia are drinking coffee, and Lola is barking happily in the background.
"Hello everyone!" I call into the camera.
"How was your week, Maya?" asks my mother.
"Very nice and quite normal," I answer.
"I cooked our family recipe yesterday evening."
"My neighbour Sabine was here for dinner."
"Did she like it?" asks my father with interest.
"Yes, she thought the food was fantastic!"
I laugh.
"And how was the sport?"
Sofia wants to know.
"Exhausting!" I say.
"I played badminton on Thursday, and it was very hot in the hall."
"Summer is really here."
"Do you still work in the café?" asks Diego.
"Yes, I sold coffee and Brötchen yesterday morning," I say.
"And how is everything going with you all in Mexico?"
We talk for almost an hour, and I feel very happy.
